  "id": "moral-commitment",
  "term": "moral commitment",
  "definition": "Moral commitment is a person’s steady dedication to ethical values that helps give desire, conduct, and emotional life an ethical direction. In the source, it is presented as part of a Confucian path of self-cultivation and psychological reorientation under suffering and instability.",
